lv_obj_report_style_change() rebuilds a widget's style cache masks for both
the MAIN part and the other parts. The walk stops at the first style that
matches, and refreshing only that style's part leaves the other mask stale
when the style also sits on another part, or when every style changed
(`style == NULL`). With LV_OBJ_STYLE_CACHE on, a property a theme rebuild
adds to an indicator or knob style then reads as its default.

diff --git a/src/core/lv_obj_style.c b/src/core/lv_obj_style.c
--- a/src/core/lv_obj_style.c
+++ b/src/core/lv_obj_style.c
@@ -1184,7 +1184,9 @@
     uint32_t i;
     for(i = 0; i < obj->style_cnt; i++) {
         if(style == NULL || obj->styles[i].style == style) {
-            full_cache_refresh(obj, lv_obj_style_get_selector_part(obj->styles[i].selector));
+            /*The loop stops at the first match, but the style can sit on several parts
+             *(and with `style == NULL` every part changed), so rebuild both masks.*/
+            full_cache_refresh(obj, LV_PART_ANY);
             lv_obj_refresh_style(obj, LV_PART_ANY, LV_STYLE_PROP_ANY);
             break;
         }
